	<item>
		<title>ROH-AEW talent holding wrestling fundraiser show for alma mater</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397205-roh-aew-talent-holding-wrestling-fundraiser-show-for-alma-mater/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397205-roh-aew-talent-holding-wrestling-fundraiser-show-for-alma-mater/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:56:04 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Deonna Purrazzo]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[ROH]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[wrestling fundraiser]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397205</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Deonna Purrazzo is set to return to her hometown for a special wrestling-centric fundraiser in support of her&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397205-roh-aew-talent-holding-wrestling-fundraiser-show-for-alma-mater/">ROH-AEW talent holding wrestling fundraiser show for alma mater</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Deonna Purrazzo is set to return to her hometown for a special wrestling-centric fundraiser in support of her alma mater high school.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In an interview with <a href="https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/ring-of-honor-champ-deonna-purrazzo-bringing-wrestling-nj-town-raise-awareness-major-issue">Fox News OutKick</a>, the AEW talent talked about the upcoming JTown SmackDown, which will put a spotlight on the lack of funding for schools in the area:</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I&#8217;ve worked with the athletic director, Bill Koch, for the past few months, since earlier this year, really, when we were reconnected over the Highlands Impact Aid Now rally at Jefferson, where we&#8217;re trying to draw attention to the fact that the funding formula for schools in New Jersey, the S-2 funding formula is not fair.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It&#8217;s not equitable to the students of the Highlands and the Pinelands. And so that kind of was the precipice to JTown SmackDown. We were raising money for the athletic department and for the JTEF, the Jefferson Township Educational Fund, which is all going to the students.</p>
</blockquote>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Purrazzo, the reigning ROH Women&#8217;s Pure Champion, will team with husband Steve Maclin to take on VSK and Emily Jaye when JTown SmackDown emanates from Jefferson Township High School in Oak Ridge on Friday, November 13.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397205-roh-aew-talent-holding-wrestling-fundraiser-show-for-alma-mater/">ROH-AEW talent holding wrestling fundraiser show for alma mater</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397205-roh-aew-talent-holding-wrestling-fundraiser-show-for-alma-mater/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>AEW Dynamite/Collision Results &#8211; 11/11/26 (Live 3-Hour Special: Go-Home Show For Full Gear, Title Match, More!)</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397168-aew-dynamite-collision-3-hour-special-11-11-26/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397168-aew-dynamite-collision-3-hour-special-11-11-26/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:05:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW Collision Results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW Dynamite Results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[11/11/26 AEW Collision Results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[11/11/26 AEW Dynamite Results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Collision]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Dynamite]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[HBO Max]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Salt Lake City]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[TBS]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Utah]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[West Valley City]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397168</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>AEW Dynamite/Collision ResultsNovember 11, 2026Maverick Center in West Valley City, (Salt Lake City) UtahResults by: Alex Kahrs and&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397168-aew-dynamite-collision-3-hour-special-11-11-26/">AEW Dynamite/Collision Results &#8211; 11/11/26 (Live 3-Hour Special: Go-Home Show For Full Gear, Title Match, More!)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>AEW Dynamite/Collision Results</strong><br><strong>November 11, 2026</strong><br><strong>Maverick Center in West Valley City, (Salt Lake City) Utah</strong><br><strong>Results by: Alex Kahrs and Jerome Wilen of Wrestleview.com</strong></p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full is-resized"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1256" height="313" src="https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_dynamite__official__logo_2024_by_wrestlerender_dh23y7w.png" alt="" class="wp-image-397209" style="aspect-ratio:4.012898602651379;width:271px;height:auto" srcset="https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_dynamite__official__logo_2024_by_wrestlerender_dh23y7w.png 1256w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_dynamite__official__logo_2024_by_wrestlerender_dh23y7w-600x150.png 600w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_dynamite__official__logo_2024_by_wrestlerender_dh23y7w-380x95.png 380w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_dynamite__official__logo_2024_by_wrestlerender_dh23y7w-550x137.png 550w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_dynamite__official__logo_2024_by_wrestlerender_dh23y7w-800x199.png 800w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aew_dynamite__official__logo_2024_by_wrestlerender_dh23y7w-1160x289.png 1160w" sizes="(max-width: 1256px) 100vw, 1256px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Commentary welcomes us to the show before running down the lineup for tonight and Full Gear. From there we go to a video package looking back at the highlights Blood and Guts last week. From Julia Hart submitting to end the women&#8217;s B&amp;G match to Cope being forced to surrender in the men&#8217;s match, only for Darby Allin to be shoved off the cage and through a stack of tables by Wardlow.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We go to footage from after the show, where Will Ospreay breaks the silence by trying to understand why Cope would break the oath the squad made to not surrender or submit. He runs down Adam by noting the kids watching him in his shirt, and whether he thought Darby wouldn&#8217;t be thrown off the cage&#8211;but Cope interrupts by addressing his own past with injury, saying he didn&#8217;t want to see that for anyone else. He speaks on the injuries the rest of the squad has suffered, and was trying to keep them from having to retire. If they can&#8217;t understand that, maybe this isn&#8217;t the place for him. He storms off as we head back to ringside.</p>



<h3 id="will-ospreay-and-kyle-fletcher-go-face-to-face" class="wp-block-heading">Will Ospreay and Kyle Fletcher go Face-To-Face</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Don Callis accompanies Kyle Fletcher to the ring as commentary talks about his match for the AEW World Championship at Full Gear. Kyle gets a microphone, and out next is Will Ospreay to a big pop from the crowd. As the champ enters the ring to pose for the fans, Kyle says to cut the music. He&#8217;s not out here to listen to this BS. This gets boos and &#8220;Ospreay&#8221; chants from the fans.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The chants turn to &#8220;f&#8211;k Don Callis,&#8221; to which Kyle asks if they&#8217;re done. He turns his attention to Ospreay, saying it&#8217;s been two years since they had a face-to-face conversation and they&#8217;re well due another. He reminds us of when he shaved his head, saying so much has happened&#8230;as the crowd tells him &#8220;you look stupid.&#8221; Kyle disagrees, realizing this is not an argument worth having as he addresses what has happened to Ospreay in that same timeframe. He got married, he got neck surgery, he came back from neck surgery, and he won the AEW World Champion.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This gets &#8220;he&#8217;s World Champion&#8221; chants, to which Fletcher congratulates the crowd on being observant before bringing up his own success in that timeframe. He wraps it up by giving Ospreay some respect and thanks. Ospreay is surprised by this, thanking Kyle and saying he&#8217;s kept his eye on him for two years&#8230;and he&#8217;s proud of Kyle. Fletcher said he is grateful for everything that&#8217;s happened since, and this is a point Kyle reiterates as he explains that he would do everything again if he could.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He comes back around to the neck injury that took Ospreay out for months&#8230;upset that Ospreay went after Jon Moxley when he came back, when it was Fletcher who dropped him on his neck over and over to take him out. He wants the credit he deserves.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ospreay admits that it was Kyle who broke his neck, addressing the pain he went through before explaining that the roar of the crowd is what kept him going when he was basically wrestling with one arm. It&#8217;s a painkiller for him, bruv. He talks about the bit that Kyle cut off moments ago, saying it&#8217;s a call to arms like the Batsignal for him. He then reminds Fletcher that even with a broken neck he beat him twice&#8230;and now, fully healed, he is wrestling at a level nobody can replicated.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He talks about outlasting seven opponents in Clockwork Carnage, beating the ace of AEW, hit a Black Arrow when the world needed it most, and beat Kenny Omega for the World Title at All In. He directs the production truck to play a clip he sent in this morning, reminding us that the last two men to see him backstage before he went out where Fletcher and Davis. He asks Kyle to tell him what he was feeling in that moment. Fletcher starts to bring up Don Callis, but Ospreay says he doesn&#8217;t want to hear Don&#8217;s words, he wants Kyle&#8217;s answer. As this goes on, there is a fan yelling out that Fletcher felt jealous, while Ospreay thinks Fletcher and Davis wanted to go out there with him like old times.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Eventually, Fletcher confirms that one fan&#8217;s theory by telling the champ that he was jealous. He was jealous that the man he hated most was about to win the biggest prize&#8230;until he realized that he had a chance to be the one to take it all away. Ospreay doesn&#8217;t believe him, saying he thinks his old pals wanted to be at ringside just like he believes deep down Fletcher still loves him. Kyle claims he never loved Will, and that he and Davis saw the truth about Ospreay. Callum Newman recently saw it, and someday everyone Ospreay ever loved will see it&#8230;including Will&#8217;s wife and son, and if his son won&#8217;t see it on his own, Fletcher will be there to tell him what kind of man Ospreay really is.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>Refresh for the latest results!</em></p>



<h3 id="dynamite-quick-results" class="wp-block-heading">Dynamite Quick Results:</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li></li>
</ul>



<h3 id="still-to-come" class="wp-block-heading">Still to Come:</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Mixed Tag:</strong> Jay White and Mercedes Moné vs. Death Riders (Jon Moxley andd Marina Shafir)</li>



<li>The New Level (Austin Creed and Kofi) vs. Brodido (Bandido and Brody King)</li>



<li><strong>AEW National Championship:</strong> Tommaso Ciampa defends against ‘Speedball’ Mike Bailey</li>



<li><strong>Match 5 of Best of Five Series:</strong> FTR (Dax Harwood and Cash Wheeler) vs. Motor City Machine Guns (Alex Shelley and Chris Sabin)</li>
</ul>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397168-aew-dynamite-collision-3-hour-special-11-11-26/">AEW Dynamite/Collision Results &#8211; 11/11/26 (Live 3-Hour Special: Go-Home Show For Full Gear, Title Match, More!)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397168-aew-dynamite-collision-3-hour-special-11-11-26/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Former WWE champion launching &#8216;Not Too Small&#8217; wrestler agency</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397202-former-wwe-champion-launching-not-too-small-wrestler-agency/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397202-former-wwe-champion-launching-not-too-small-wrestler-agency/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:56:55 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Misc. News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Chavo Guerrero]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[wrestling agency]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397202</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>In an interview with Fightful, Chavo Guerrero Jr. gave details on the launch of Not Too Small, a&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397202-former-wwe-champion-launching-not-too-small-wrestler-agency/">Former WWE champion launching &#8216;Not Too Small&#8217; wrestler agency</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In an interview with <a href="https://www.fightful.com/wrestling/338615-chavo-guerrero-brad-small-agency/">Fightful</a>, Chavo Guerrero Jr. gave details on the launch of Not Too Small, a talent agency in partnership with longtime wrestling attorney Brad Small.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Guerrero, a former WWE Cruiserweight Champion who has since worked for the likes of TNA, Lucha Underground, AEW, and more, explained the history behind launching the agency, aiming to negotiate wrestling contracts and help wrestlers land deals in ventures outside pro wrestling itself:</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Brad Small, he’s been my lawyer/agent since 2003, doing most of my WWE/WWF stuff and of course, all my TNA and Lucha stuff. Definitely all of my Hollywood stuff. Brad’s just — he’s represented all the big players in the industry and we were talking, with his connections and my connections, why are we not representing wrestlers on our own and doing our own agency? That got us thinking, it was a little while back we started talking about that. He was all for it — I just think it’s such a great fit because what happens in this industry, you have people trying to represent wrestlers but first of all, if you don’t know wrestling contracts, they’re a whole different ball game. It’s an own set, it’s got its own place in contracts. Anybody from Hollywood trying to read a wrestling contract would be like, hell no, no way, don’t ever sign that. I’ve heard that time and time again from wrestlers trying to get a new guy doing their contacts, that’s just not how it works.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">So, you really have to know contracts. Brad Small knows contacts. Then, with all the Hollywood stuff that we’ve got going on, that I’ve got going on, people that’s he’s represented like Eva Longoria and Chris Jericho, man it was just like a perfect fit. So, we created our agency called Not Too Small, playing off his name and our Guerrero size. We’ve always been not too small, but we’re too small in a big man’s business [laughs].</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">That’s what’s going on man, we created our own agency and we’re going to represent wrestlers not only in the wrestling world but also transitioning into the Hollywood world or in other business ventures like brand endorsements and really anything that they want to do to kind of make their brand bigger. There’s a couple of other people in that space, but I just feel that we really just have so much to offer. Talking to Tony Khan, right away he got back to us and was like, ‘Wow, this is really great.’ A couple other people from WWE got back to us and it was pretty cool to hear their feedback.</p>
</blockquote>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<iframe title="Chavo Guerrero Announces New Agency, Talks Maculay Culkin, Working With Spielberg, Lucha UG" width="1200" height="675" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/NuRt44ygod4?start=1187&amp;feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397202-former-wwe-champion-launching-not-too-small-wrestler-agency/">Former WWE champion launching &#8216;Not Too Small&#8217; wrestler agency</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397202-former-wwe-champion-launching-not-too-small-wrestler-agency/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Ludwig Kaiser&#8217;s legal counsel files &#8220;Motion to Compel&#8221; to seek alleged victim’s medical records in battery case</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397193-ludwig-kaisers-legal-counsel-files-motion-to-compel-to-seek-alleged-victims-medical-records-in-battery-case/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397193-ludwig-kaisers-legal-counsel-files-motion-to-compel-to-seek-alleged-victims-medical-records-in-battery-case/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:46:04 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Ludwig Kaiser]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Motion to Compel]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397193</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>According to a new report from F4WOnline, Ludwig Kaiser (real name Marcel Barthel) and his defense are still&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397193-ludwig-kaisers-legal-counsel-files-motion-to-compel-to-seek-alleged-victims-medical-records-in-battery-case/">Ludwig Kaiser&#8217;s legal counsel files &#8220;Motion to Compel&#8221; to seek alleged victim’s medical records in battery case</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">According to a <a href="https://www.f4wonline.com/news/wwe/ludwig-kaiser-files-motion-seeking-alleged-victims-medical-records-in-battery-case/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">new report from F4WOnline</a>, Ludwig Kaiser (real name Marcel Barthel) and his defense are still making attempt to gain access to potentially important evidence in the ongoing battery case against the WWE/AAA talent.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The report notes a “Motion to Compel” was filed on Tuesday, November 10 with Kaiser’s defense asking for the court to direct the Office of the State Attorney to hand over all medical records pertaining to the injuries suffered by Richard Reap, the alleged victim. It is further noted that within the filing, the defense for Kaiser argues that being able to review the medical records could show evidence Reap did not suffer the injuries he claims or that the injuries did happen, but are unrelated to the incident.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">F4WOnline further states that Assistant State Attorney Juanda Padgett <a href="https://www.f4wonline.com/news/wwe/ludwig-kaisers-defense-given-access-to-medical-records/">initially agreed to share the medical records</a> with Kaiser’s defense back in late October. However, Padgett did not send the records due to Reap’s attorney due to objecting to the idea. Reap has hired his own legal counsel, potentially indicating he could be planning a civil case against Kaiser after the criminal matter is resolved. At the present time, Kaiser is facing a misdemeanor battery charge as a result of incident between himself and Reap which happened in and then just outside of an elevator at the apartment complex Kaiser was living in at the time in Orlando, Florida.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Another pre-trial conference is scheduled for December 17, with a possible trial that could take place January 4-22, 2027, if the case does not get extended or end in a plead agreement before those dates.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Reap has accused Kaiser of attacking him following the elevator stopping at Reap’s floor. Both Kaiser and Reap do agree the altercation took place after Reap had asked Kaiser and his girlfriend Andrea Bazarte to “please have some manners,” as they were getting overly affectionate with each other in the same elevator Reap was on. Kaiser claims Reap swore at him, the made a racist comment that involved contacting ICE on Bazarte. Kaiser has admitted to pushing Reap, but said that he only did it after Reap aggressively lunged towards him and then made threats – all while in the elevator.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The original arrest report notes local police viewed the surveillance video from inside the building and could see Kaiser punching and pushing Reap. The report also indicates that police did see a scratch on Reaps head.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Kaiser entered a “not guilty” plea in response to the misdemeanor battery charge. Kaiser&#8217;s defense had  made attempts to get the case dismissed under Florida’s “Stand Your Ground” law, with the claim Kasier&#8217;s use of non-deadly force against Reap was justified in order to protect himself and Bazarte against “imminent use of unlawful force.”</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Kaiser, under the El Grande Americano gimmick, is the current AAA Mega Champion. He won the title after defeating <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dominik_Mysterio">Dominik Mysterio</a> in a No Disqualification Match on the second night of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tripleman%C3%ADa_34">Triplemanía 34</a> back on September 13, 2026.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397193-ludwig-kaisers-legal-counsel-files-motion-to-compel-to-seek-alleged-victims-medical-records-in-battery-case/">Ludwig Kaiser&#8217;s legal counsel files &#8220;Motion to Compel&#8221; to seek alleged victim’s medical records in battery case</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397193-ludwig-kaisers-legal-counsel-files-motion-to-compel-to-seek-alleged-victims-medical-records-in-battery-case/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>TKO employees reportedly frustrated over safety issues with UFC and WWE events in Saudi Arabia</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397190-tko-employees-reportedly-frustrated-over-safety-issues-with-ufc-and-wwe-events-in-saudi-arabia/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397190-tko-employees-reportedly-frustrated-over-safety-issues-with-ufc-and-wwe-events-in-saudi-arabia/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:42:54 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[employees]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[events]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Saudi Arabia]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[TKO]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[UFC]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397190</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>According to a report from Ben Fowlkes of Uncrowned, TKO employees are reportedly frustrated with the parent company&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397190-tko-employees-reportedly-frustrated-over-safety-issues-with-ufc-and-wwe-events-in-saudi-arabia/">TKO employees reportedly frustrated over safety issues with UFC and WWE events in Saudi Arabia</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">According to a report from <a href="https://sports.yahoo.com/mma/article/inside-tkos-saudi-arabia-crisis-ufc-wwe-workers-speak-out-as-safety-fears-escalate-everyone-just-cant-believe-this-020000151.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Ben Fowlkes of Uncrowned</a>, TKO employees are reportedly frustrated with the parent company of WWE and UFC moving forward with events in Saudi Arabia despite ongoing military conflict in the country. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fowlkes notes sources told Uncrowned that several of TKO&#8217;s employees have grown increasingly frustrated at the company&#8217;s insistence on going through with events in Riyadh even when missile and drone attacks by the Houthi militia in Yemen continue. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A recent attack happened in Riyadh&#8217;s financial district just hours after Saturday&#8217;s WWE Crown Jewel event ended. While it was confirmed in other reports that WWE Superstars left by the time a missile struck a tower owned by the state-run Aramco oil company on Sunday, some of TKO&#8217;s employees said they felt their safety has been little more than an afterthought.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A source, speaking on the condition of anonymity due to fear of reprisal, told Uncrowned, &#8220;Why are you still even having these shows at this point?&#8221; I think the answer is, if they chose not to do the show, they would lose out on millions and millions of dollars.&#8221; The source continued on by saying, &#8220;If we don&#8217;t do the shows in Saudi Arabia or [United Arab Emirates] or Doha or wherever we are going, then our fourth-quarter earnings will be off and our shareholders aren&#8217;t going to get their money So it&#8217;s all about greed. They don&#8217;t care about anybody&#8217;s well-being. The level of greed with this company is so gross.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Uncrowned reached out to TKO representatives for comment regarding safety concerns expressed by its employees and the decision to move forward with events in Saudi Arabia. Uncrowned notes at the time of their report, TKO did not respond. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A source inside TKO told Uncrowned, &#8220;All [TKO executives] talk about is if the State Department says it is OK to fly there. The rest of us are like, &#8216;If the State Department has to think about it at all, let&#8217;s just postpone.&#8217; That&#8217;s what all the other sports are doing. Why can&#8217;t TKO?&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ahead of a UFC Fight Night event planned to be held in Riyadh on December 5, some TKO employees told Uncrowned they are increasingly upset with what they see as a disregard for employee safety and a lack of communication about potential contingency plans.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">&#8220;Not one email has gone out saying, &#8216;Here are the details and the plans for December 5th.&#8217; That&#8217;s crazy,&#8221; said one source. &#8220;They don&#8217;t tell you anything. They just throw it at you. How about a backup plan? How about a safety letter? &#8216;Hey, if x happens, we go do y. We&#8217;ll all meet here. We&#8217;ll do this. We&#8217;ll do that.&#8217; Nothing.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Furthermore, now, with added concerns regarding the continued ongoing military conflict, some within TKO have stated that executive leadership is not taking their safety seriously enough.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A source told Uncrowned, TKO does not care about about their employees and people within the company are tired of how they are being treated. &#8220;They don&#8217;t f&#8212;&#8211;g care about you one bit. People are just getting tired of the way they&#8217;re getting treated. They get treated like s&#8211; and everybody&#8217;s tired of it. The lack of communication, the greed, the lack of appreciation, people are just sick of it.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Other sources have told Uncrowned that events in Saudi Arabia and the risks that come with traveling and working from what is essentially an active conflict zone, have pushed some off TKO&#8217;s employees to their breaking point. One longtime TKO employee told Uncrowned the mood among staff had darkened after the company refused to move or postpone events even after airports had been attacked in Saudi Arabia. It was added that some of the employees under the TKO banner have said communication from top executives has been lacking, despite during a recent company town hall meeting, Mark Shapiro, TKO&#8217;s President and Chief Operating assured employees the company would &#8220;not hesitate&#8221; to cancel or postpone events in the region in the face of &#8220;danger or a further escalation&#8221; in the military conflict.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Also during the company town hall meeting, Shapiro acknowledged canceling the events in Saudi Arabia would impact business in &#8220;a very negative way,&#8221; but then said &#8220;business is secondary&#8221; to employee safety. However, Shapiro added TKO is currently on track for an lucrative year financially, which was noted in the company&#8217;s <a href="https://sports.yahoo.com/mma/article/tko-reports-136-billion-in-q3-revenue-with-ufc-alone-pulling-in-5192-million-from-july-to-september-221454928.html">third-quarter earnings repor</a>t, which included an increased targeted revenue of $5.83 billion for the year.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A source, speaking on the condition of anonymity, told Uncrowned, &#8220;Everyone is talking about the Middle East shows, Who has to go, who can get out of going. Some people say they are waiting until the time to fly comes and telling [executives] that they won&#8217;t go. But I don&#8217;t know how many will follow through with that. This is a company that can fire you for no reason or any reason. Everyone just can&#8217;t believe this is a choice that they are being forced to make — fly into a war zone or risk getting fired before Christmas.&#8221; Former and current employees described a company culture at that is shortsighted and focused on maximizing short-term profitability, with little regard for employees who keep the company going. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">One source told Uncrowned, &#8220;We&#8217;ve come to the realization, this is what it is. We&#8217;re going to either have to accept it or leave, because nothing&#8217;s going to change at this point. But it&#8217;s time to get called out. People think it&#8217;s fine and you get taken care of. People realize the fighters get paid s&#8212;. I mean, that&#8217;s obvious. You guys have covered that aspect of it. People know, and the fighters are starting to speak up for themselves, but it doesn&#8217;t stop with them. That&#8217;s the message I want to get across. Everyone across the whole company gets treated like s&#8212;, whether you&#8217;re a fighter or a camera guy.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A report this past Tuesday from <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397061-report-update-on-scrapped-wwe-crown-jewel-match/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">F4WOnline</a> noted a match between Gunther and Finn Balor was ultimately dropped from Crown Jewel&#8217;s lineup because Gunther decided against traveling to Saudi Arabia. However it was also noted that Balor had reservations about making the trip, but the belief internally was that he would have traveled had Gunther agreed to participate.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397190-tko-employees-reportedly-frustrated-over-safety-issues-with-ufc-and-wwe-events-in-saudi-arabia/">TKO employees reportedly frustrated over safety issues with UFC and WWE events in Saudi Arabia</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397190-tko-employees-reportedly-frustrated-over-safety-issues-with-ufc-and-wwe-events-in-saudi-arabia/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
